# Module — Amazon Webservice proxy

Amazon legacy (`Prestashop-Amazon`) and Amazon SaaS (`Prestashop-SAAS-Module`) both call SP-API through the **Amazon-Webservice** proxy.

Production base URL: `https://amazon-webservice.common-services.com`, from `AmazonWebserviceConnector::proxyEndpoint()` in each module's `classes/webservice/`. Paths are the constants in `classes/webservice/AmazonWebserviceAPI.php` (orders V2026, feeds, reports, catalog, and the rest).

## Source of truth

| Role | Path |
|---|---|
| **Proxy (source of truth)** | `/var/www/projects/shopify/Amazon-Webservice` |
| Cron app (not this proxy) | `/var/www/projects/prestashop/Prestashop-SAAS` — `https://amz-saas-ps.common-services.com/api` |

On Windows/WSL, edit `/var/www/projects/shopify/Amazon-Webservice`. Do not treat `C:\Users\Windows 10\projects\shopify\Amazon-Webservice` as the running copy; it can be stale.

A change there is not deployed until that proxy is deployed. A module ZIP does not contain this app.

`module-saas-webservice.mdc` covers `Prestashop-SAAS` only.

## Legacy `seller_partner/`

`classes/seller_partner/` still has the old proxy `https://mwsops2.common-services.com/`. Do not add new SP-API behaviour there.

Route mapping stays in `Prestashop-SAAS-Module/documentation/common-services/proxy-api-types.md`. Read that file. Do not copy the route table into this rule.

## Where to edit

| Need | Edit |
|---|---|
| Request the module sends | That module's `classes/webservice/` |
| Allow-list, validation, or SP-API mapping on the proxy | `/var/www/projects/shopify/Amazon-Webservice` |

Do not "fix" a proxy reject by editing only the module, and do not invent proxy behaviour from a stale checkout.
